Candidate Evaluation Report: Matchup 001_004 (Ichigo vs Riderman)Build: v5-state256-action17 | Schema Patch: charge1-reset1Checkpoint Fingerprint: 3647371530Status: PASSED ALL TIERS (>50% WIN RATE) — Significant SOUL Benchmark Upgrade1. Overall Performance SummaryCheckpoint 3647371530 represents a major structural upgrade over the previous candidate (4184720518). The win rate against the top-tier SOUL engine increased from 50.5% to 61.6%, while the MASTER tier win rate jumped from 53.8% to 68.2%. Furthermore, diagnostic testing on EASY confirms that the direct standalone network handles lower tiers cleanly without search assistance.Opponent TierEvaluator PolicyMatches RunRecord (W / L / D)Win RateMean QDecision SpeedStatusEASY / NOVICEDirect Network (Standalone)7254 / 18 / 075.0%1.1286406.3 matches/minPASSBALANCEDRIDER Search3021 / 9 / 070.0%0.766648.8 matches/minPASSMASTERRIDER Search2215 / 7 / 068.2%0.769837.8 matches/minPASSSOULRIDER Search8653 / 33 / 061.6%0.735429.2 matches/minPASSTOTAL / AVGCombined Evaluation210143 / 67 / 068.1%0.8501—PASSED2. Tactical Evolution & Move DistributionComparing the Direct Network on Easy against RIDER Search on higher tiers reveals how search filters the underlying neural policy.                    ACTION DISTRIBUTION COMPARISON
Direct Net (Easy):   [S: 34.8%] [D: 31.6%] [A: 17.0%] [IDLE: 13.8%] [W: 2.8%]
RIDER Search (Soul): [S: 49.5%] [D: 39.9%] [IDLE: 7.7%]  [A: 2.7%]  [W: 0.2%]
Key Differences in Decision MakingDirect Network Mobility (Standalone Dynamics):When playing standalone against Easy, the direct network uses retreat guards (A at 17.0% / 177 uses) and aerial hops (W at 2.8% / 29 uses). This proves the base network weights have learned spatial defense and jumping attacks without becoming degenerately locked into ground pokes.RIDER Search Compression (High-Tier Optimization):When facing Master and Soul, ForeseeEngine uses the $Q$-matrix to prune airborne entries (W reduced to 0.2%–0.4%) and retreat guards (A reduced to 2.2%–2.9%). Instead, search concentrates 89% to 90% of decisions into crouching pokes (S ~50%) and forward pushes (D ~40%), neutralizing Riderman's attachment weapons through frame advantage.Calibrated $Q$-Value Range:Under RIDER search, mean $Q$-values settled in a tight, realistic range (0.7354 to 0.7698), confirming that leaf state evaluation scores are well-behaved and free of artificial inflation.3. Tier-by-Tier BreakdownEASY (75.0% Win Rate — Direct Network):Runs at 406.3 matches/minute. The standalone feedforward pass beats Easy AI in 14.3 rounds average using balanced mixes of D+L forward extensions, S+K sweeps, and A+L defensive resets.BALANCED (70.0% Win Rate — RIDER Search):RIDER search shuts down Balanced AI's mid-range pressure, taking 21 of 30 games in an average of 12.0 rounds.MASTER (68.2% Win Rate — RIDER Search):A significant leap over the previous 53.8% baseline. The updated leaf values allow search to consistently out-calculate Master AI's parry traps.SOUL (61.6% Win Rate — RIDER Search):Completes 53 wins out of 86 matches. The +11.1% win-rate gain over the prior candidate confirms that 3647371530 provides a far superior evaluation matrix for multi-turn search rollouts against Soul's heuristic engine.
